As Finn says, your eigen-implementation implicitly uses two constraints, sum(x)=0 and sum((1:n)*x) = 0, which are the two Eigen vectors with zero eigenvalues.
INLA by default, only use sum(x), so you need to add the linear one, explicitely using extraconstr

H

